IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Sex Discrimination Act 1984 (Cth), baseline 2026-11 -- the one module that imports daydate.
-- The other modules and the case files take their dates from here, so that daydate is imported once.

§ `Dates`

-- A calendar date, day first. `Date` rolls an impossible date forward (`the date` 29 2 2023 is 1 March 2023).
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` d m y MEANS Date d m y

-- A date a whole number of months later, with the day clamped to the end of a shorter month (daydate's `add months`:
-- 29 February 2024 plus 24 months is 28 February 2026).
GIVEN start IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`months after` start n MEANS `add months` start n

-- Act No. 85, 2022 (Anti-Discrimination and Human Rights Legislation Amendment (Respect at Work) Act 2022) added Part IIA
-- (s 47C), s 8A and s 28M. The compilation's endnote 3 gives its commencement as "Sch 1, Sch 2 (items 1-13), Sch 7 (item
-- 16) and Sch 8 (items 2, 3): 13 Dec 2022 (s 2(1) items 2, 3, 6)". The endnote does not say which item inserted which
-- section; that all three came in on 13 December 2022 is read from it (see NOTES.md, finding 1).
`Respect at Work 2022 commencement` MEANS `the date` 13 12 2022
